[{"id":3559939439,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7UMF1v","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"99b889b6c3d13d76e29582682d69a049a153a041","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it mostly works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\nUndo/redo isn't working very consistently though. It will work in simple scenarios (assign material then undo), but if you perform multiple drag-and-drops, the first undo operation will appear to do nothing, then the second undo operation will revert to the state before either of the materials were drag-and-dropped:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/753965a6-8567-45f0-994e-539709e1dbf2\r\n\r\nNote that you need to right-click the 3D editor viewport once after the second drag-and-drop so that it gets focus (otherwise, undo will affect the text in the shader editor).\r\n\r\n","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113748#pullrequestreview-3559939439","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113748","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-12-09T22:06:42Z"},{"id":3560022112,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7UMaBg","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"99b889b6c3d13d76e29582682d69a049a153a041","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4M